    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d319">

                <pb facs="0502" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1863p1/pg460"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Stuart.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1862-11-11"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 11, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> The instruction of the 16th ultimo from the
                    British Foreign Office, in relation to the case of Mr. Francis Carroll, which
                    you recently left at this de partment, and which is herewith returned to you,
                    having been communicated to Major L.C. Turner, associate judge advocate, I now
                    have the honor to enclose to you a copy of his reply. It will be seen that an
                    order has been issued by the War Department for Mr. Carroll’s discharge, in
                    conformity with the terms suggested by this government, and acceded to by that
                    of her Britannic Majesty.</p>
                <p>I have the honour to be, with high consideration, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William Stuart</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>



                <xi:include href="d319-a1.xml" xpointer="d319-a1"/>
